    "findings": [
      "ALL 18 rebound and loaded (0 ERR): the earlier rejection was identity fingerprint only, never payload.",
      "read 0xC3C8 4 is answerable in every state (4 bytes returned; zeros in non-battle states).",
      "The load-time state does NOT identify the action: 11 of 14 distinct states share an identical base-position AND animation-slot block, so card/side cannot be read off at load time.",
      "Non-battle states (C0A0=02, all-zero base/slots): list-base, list-gohan, nav1/battle-checkpoint - not ACTION-capable.",
      "Playing each state with input 60:1:8: kame_left_base and tail_left_base/tail_left_move START an action (obj0 baseX 0x28->0x58, one animation-slot register changes); pc_left_base and every offense/base state do NOT start an action under this input.",
      "The distinguishing register between the kame and tail states is animation slot 6 (0x62,0x94 vs 0x64,0x48). Naming the card from that register needs a slot decoder that does not exist yet, so card ids beyond card 12 are NOT receipted from the state."
    ]
  },
  "anchorModelConclusion": {
    "status": "DOCUMENTED - not implemented (shared-code hold)",
    "statement": "The ACTION anchor is wrong as a MODEL, not merely as a value. Measured across a 700-frame replay of the card-12 bootstrap: obj0 base = (baseY 96, baseX 40) over frames 0..106, (96, 88) over 107..292, a 16-frame RAMP 87->61 at frames 293..308 (one distinct value per frame), then (96, 61) over 309..489; obj1 baseX holds 136 until it jumps to 105 at frame 490. So the ROM base position is CONSTANT inside the beam window (408..487, the window 3g.1 measured: 0 change points) but demonstrably ANIMATES elsewhere in the same film.",
    "consequence": "A bare global constant (ACTION_GROUND_Y = 72 / ACTION_PLANE_GEOMETRY.home.player = {x:48,y:72}) cannot express this: it is correct for at most one beat of one card. The correct model is the FILM carrying the ROM base position per beat (base read at $C3C8..$C3CB, rendered = base + animation frame offset, per src/battle/romActionObject.ts positionModel), with the anchor constant as a fallback rather than an authority.",
    "therefore": [
      "No ACTION_OBJECT_POSITION cue emission is needed for 408..487: the base is constant there, so a cue would carry a constant and add surface on an 83-card shared path for zero fidelity gain.",
      "The anchor conversion alone fixes the proven (-5,+16) divergence inside that window.",
      "A per-beat position cue IS the right model for the beats where the base animates (e.g. 293..308), but that is a separate change and remains held.",
      "Blast radius remains family-wide (83 cards / 5 profile kinds) and only 1 of 83 is currently capturable, so the family needs baseline captures before any global change."
    ],
